1. Leaderboard — missing index on quest_completions.apprentice_id:
CREATE INDEX ON quest_completions (apprentice_id);
This allows an Index Scan on the JOIN instead of a Seq Scan. For read-heavy leaderboards, also consider a materialized view refreshed every 5 minutes.

2. Spell search — leading wildcard LIKE cannot use B-tree:
Option A: Add full-text search:
ALTER TABLE spells ADD COLUMN search_vec tsvector
  GENERATED ALWAYS AS (to_tsvector('english', description)) STORED;
CREATE INDEX ON spells USING GIN (search_vec);
SELECT title FROM spells WHERE search_vec @@ plainto_tsquery('english', 'wizard');

Option B: If exact substring is required: pg_trgm extension + GIN trigram index:
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm;
CREATE INDEX ON spells USING GIN (description gin_trgm_ops);
Now LIKE '%wizard%' can use the index.

3. Rolling sum — replace correlated subquery with window function + RANGE frame:
SELECT date, xp,
  SUM(xp) OVER (
    ORDER BY date
    RANGE BETWEEN INTERVAL '30 days' PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW
  ) AS rolling_30d
FROM xp_log;
This is O(n) vs O(n²) for the correlated subquery.
